\begin_layout Standard
## Invariance under basis transformations
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In [](matrix-operations) we attached several quantities to a square matrix: the trace, the determinant and the characteristic polynomial. In 
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
{
\end_layout

\end_inset

ref
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
}
\end_layout

\end_inset

`trace-det-basis-invariant`, you will check that the trace and the determinant are invariant under basis transformation: if 
\begin_inset Formula $A$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 are square matrices of the same size with 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 invertible, then we have
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\begin_inset Formula \[
\tr(PAP^{-1})=\tr A
\quad\text{and}\quad
\det(PAP^{-1})=\det A.
\]
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Because the characteristic polynomial is also defined as a determinant, it too is invariant under basis transformation.
\end_layout

